<title>BELGIUM: EU raises 1996 beet sugar crop to 15.63 mln tns.</title>
<headline>EU raises 1996 beet sugar crop to 15.63 mln tns.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union raised on Thursday its forecast for the 1996 beet sugar crop to 15.63 million tonnes, from 15.42 million on September 30.</p>
<p>Production was 15.64 million tonnes in 1995.</p>
<p>The forecast, which was circulated at a meeting of the EU sugar management committee on Wednesday, was based on a higher average white sugar yield of 7.76 tonnes per hectare, compared with 7.70 tonnes in September.</p>
<p>The sugar area was left unchanged from last month at 2.01 million hectares.</p>
<p>&quot;Production figures are creeping up because of the good autumn weather. More changes can be expected as it is still early in the harvest period,&quot; a trade source said.</p>
<p>Cane sugar production in French overseas territories and Spain was put at 280, 000 tonnes, unchanged from September, but up from 257,000 tonnes in 1995.</p>
<p>Molasses output was put at 19,000 tonnes, unchanged from September and last year.</p>
<p>EU sugar production was given as:</p>
<p>(million tonnes unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>			    1996/97   1996/97     1995/96</p>
<p>			    Oct 17	Sept 30</p>
<p> 1.  Area (mln/ha)     2.014	2.014	  2.086</p>
<p> 2.  White Sugar</p>
<p>     Yield (t/ha)	7.76	 7.70	   7.50</p>
<p> 3.  Beet output	15.629     15.417	  15.636</p>
<p>     Cane output	 0.280	0.280	   0.257</p>
<p>     Molasses output   0.019	0.019	   0.019</p>
<p>     Total output     15.928     15.799	  15.912</p>
<p> 4.  Carryover from</p>
<p>     pvs season	  0.685	0.685	   0.535</p>
<p> 5.  Total supplies</p>
<p>	    (3+4)	 16.613     16.484	  16.447</p>
<p> 6.  Of which</p>
<p>	&quot;A&quot; Quota	 11.724     11.724	  11.723</p>
<p>	&quot;B&quot; Quota	  2.357	2.359	   2.405</p>
<p>	&quot;C&quot; Non-Quota    2.532	2.401	   2.319</p>
<p>Of which:</p>
<p>Carry forward</p>
<p>  to next season	 0.900	0.900	   0.683</p>
<p>  Non-Quota exports    1.632	1.501	   1.636</p>
<p> 7. Consumption	  12.600    12.600	  12.650</p>
<p>(Rounded figures)</p>
